  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "28db8ac3-5ab8-43bb-8cdb-6ae80fb6aba8",
    "name": "Newman",
    "description": "## Newman – MCP Conversation Flow Tests\n\nThis collection contains end-to-end scenario tests for an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server running locally at `http://localhost:8765/mcp`. It is designed to validate conversational booking workflows — covering happy paths, ambiguous inputs, and error-handling edge cases.\n\n### Scenarios\n\n**Scenario 1 – Happy Path (Chained, Same Session)**\nA two-step flow that simulates a successful service booking within a single session:\n- **1a – Oil Change Request**: Initiates a booking request for an oil change service.\n- **1b – Confirm Booking (Same Session)**: Confirms the booking captured in the previous step, validating that session state is correctly maintained across chained requests.\n\n**Scenario 2 – Ambiguous Booking**\n- **2 – Vague Request (No Service or Time)**: Submits an underspecified booking request (missing service type and/or time) to verify that the MCP server correctly handles ambiguous or incomplete input.\n\n**Scenario 3 – Cancellation Error (Unknown Confirmation ID)**\n- **3 – Cancel With Captured (Non-Existent) Confirmation ID**: Attempts to cancel a booking using a confirmation ID that does not exist, validating that the server returns an appropriate error response.\n\n### Usage\nAll requests are `POST` to the local MCP endpoint. Run the collection sequentially (e.g. via Newman or the Collection Runner) to exercise the full range of booking conversation flows.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "11772079"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Scenario 1 - Happy Path (Chained, Same Session)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1a - Oil Change Request",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "",
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const json  = pm.response.json();",
                  "const result = json.result.structuredContent.result;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('status is awaiting_input', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(result.status).to.eql('awaiting_input');",
                  "})",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('action is create_appointment', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(result.action).to.eql('create_appointment');",
                  "})",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('needed_info is correct', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(result.details.needed_info).to.eql([\"timeslot_confirmation\"])",
                  "})"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Generate a unique session ID and persist it so request 1b reuses it",
                  "const sessionId = 'session-' + Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 10);",
                  "      pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', sessionId)"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
